G-code export: chain copies of the print's infill and support paths.

GCode::extrude_infill and extrude_support chain the print's own extrusion
entities with chain_and_reorder_extrusion_entities, which reverses some of
them in place. The Print keeps them reversed, so exporting G-code again from
the same Print (desktop does after a speed or temperature change; the
browser engine keeps the last slice's Print) printed them the other way
round, and every export of an unchanged Print differed. Chaining clones, as
ExtrusionEntityCollection::chained_path_from already does, leaves the print
as it was; the first export's G-code is unchanged.

